2026-10-05  Tomonori Kouya  <tkouya@gmail.com>

	* tools/bench_gpu_fixed.cu: skip the warp-staged variant ("n/a") when
	cu_fwarp_prepare cannot provide its shared memory, instead of launching
	with none (illegal memory access for 4096-bit complex on a GB10, whose
	99 KB per block is below the 132 KB of 4 warps x 32 elements).

2026-10-04  Tomonori Kouya  <tkouya@gmail.com>

	Release 0.0.2 (continued): x86-64 host and GPU speed of the
	fixed-precision types (checked on Xeon Gold 6526Y + H100 NVL), still
	bit-exact with MPFR/MPC.

	* include/mpc_cuda/cu_freal.cuh: x86-64 BMI2+ADX multiply kernel
	(mulx with adcx/adox carry chains, offsets as assembler symbols):
	fully unrolled up to CU_FP_X86_UNROLL_MAX_N (33) limbs, bit-identical
	to the generic kernel; above that rows padded to quads and grouped by
	length (keeps the mulhigh error bound).  Used from 4 limbs
	(CU_FP_X86_MULX_MIN_N).  cu_add_n/cu_sub_n: straight-line adc/sbb
	chain on x86-64 by default from 4 limbs (CU_FP_X86_ADC_MIN_N; replaces
	the opt-in CU_FP_X86_ASM loop).
	Device: cu_mul_cols kernel (32-bit comba with fused mad.lo.cc/madc.hi.cc,
	any start column), cu_fmul mulhigh on the GPU for 256..2048-bit;
	operands picked by value instead of by a conditional reference
	(cu_sel2 / CU_FP_SELECT2, up to CU_FP_DEV_SEL_MAX_LIMBS = 128 limbs),
	which kept both operands in local memory;
	the runtime-shift normalization of a deep cancellation works on a copy.
	Even limb counts are 16-byte aligned (128-bit loads, size unchanged).
	* include/mpc_cuda/cu_fcomplex.cuh: cu_fmmas_short, a branch-free
	fixed-point a*b +- c*d for short operands (host N <= 2, device
	N <= 32); truncated-product path usable on the device (off by
	default); by-value operand selection on the device; finalize() gets a
	copy of a wide term.
	* include/mpc_cuda/cu_ffused.cuh: cu_dot_core adds/subtracts each
	term branch-free and places the shifted product without branching on
	the bit offset.
	* include/mpc_cuda/cu_fwarp.cuh (new, included by mpc_cuda.cuh):
	cu_warp_load / cu_warp_store, warp-cooperative coalesced transfer of
	arrays of the fixed-precision types through a per-warp shared-memory
	buffer of 32 elements (cu_fwarp_buf; dynamic: cu_fwarp_dyn,
	cu_fwarp_prepare), 16-byte words for 16-byte-aligned types.
	* tools/fixed_testgen.h (new, from test_freal_host.cpp),
	tools/test_fixed_gpu.cu (new): device vs host on rounding corner
	cases, and cu_fwarp transfers (partial tiles, sentinels past n); Makefile targets check-fixed-gpu (run by check-fixed) and
	check-fixed-host now also with -march=native.
	* tools/bench_gpu_fixed.cu, tools/bench_gpu_fixed_cpu.cpp,
	tools/bench_gpu_fixed.h (new): GPU vs all CPU cores (cu_freal host,
	FLINT nfloat), each operation also with cu_fwarp transfers;
	Makefile target bench-gpu-fixed.
	* tools/bench_host_fixed.cpp: the three libraries timed in interleaved
	rounds; warm-up before the first rows.
	* tools/tune_host_fixed.sh: variants default/noasm/gmp; note on FLINT
	builds without ADX assembly.

2026-10-04  Tomonori Kouya  <tkouya@gmail.com>

	Release 0.0.2 (continued): host (CPU) speed of the fixed-precision types.

	* include/mpc_cuda/cu_freal.cuh: branch-free RNDN rounding and 0/1-bit
	  renormalization (round_up, round_make, round_inplace); cu_sum_round
	  (add/sub of normalized multi-limb terms, optional error-window check);
	  fused two-pass cu_addsub_near; cu_add_n/cu_sub_n (aarch64 adcs/sbcs,
	  opt-in x86-64 adc/sbb); host multiply kernels cu_mul_cols<N,K>
	  (mulhigh by dropping columns < K) with size-dependent shapes and an
	  optional GMP kernel; host cu_fmul as a mulhigh with exact fallback;
	  cu_round_fixed (round an approximate fixed-point value with an error
	  bound).  Device paths unchanged.
	* include/mpc_cuda/cu_fcomplex.cuh: host truncated-product fmma/fmms
	  with an error-window test, and a fixed-point Karatsuba complex
	  multiply, both with exact fallback.
	* include/mpc_cuda/cu_ffused.cuh (new): correctly rounded cu_ffma_cr,
	  cu_fdot, cu_cfma_cr, cu_cdot, and the fast mul+add cu_ffma,
	  cu_cfma; included from mpc_cuda.cuh.
	* configure.ac, Makefile.in, mpc_cuda.pc.in: CUDA optional; CPU-only
	  mode (--without-cuda or no nvcc) with targets host, check-host,
	  check-fmath-host, sample-fixed-host, install-host.
	* include/mpc_cuda_host.h, demos/sample_fixed_host.cpp,
	  tools/cuda_host_shim.h (new); tools/test_f*math*.cu also build as C++.
	* tools/test_freal_host.cpp, tools/bench_host_fixed.cpp,
	  tools/tune_host_fixed.sh (new); Makefile targets check-fixed-host and
	  bench-host-fixed.

2026-07-02  Tomonori Kouya  <tkouya@gmail.com>

	Release 0.0.2.

	* src/cuda_minigmp.cu (cu_mpn_mul): dispatch equal-size device multiplies
	  of 4..32 limbs to a new register-resident, fully-unrolled 32-bit
	  product-scanning (comba) base multiply (cu_mpn_mul_comba32<N>), which
	  keeps the whole product in registers and streams it to the destination
	  instead of accumulating through the global-memory arena with a runtime
	  limb count.  4.4x-24.5x faster for 512..2048-bit on H100 (sm_90),
	  bit-identical to the previous path; guarded by CU_MPN_MUL_NO_COMBA.
	* tests/test_combamul.cu, tests/test_combaperf.cu: correctness and
	  throughput tests for the new base multiply.

2026-06-05  Tomonori Kouya  <tkouya@gmail.com>

	Release 0.0.1.

	* Initial public release of mpc_cuda: the GNU multiple-precision stack
	  (mini-gmp -> MPFR 4.2.2 -> MPC 1.4.1) running inside CUDA kernels,
	  produced by re-runnable transform scripts (tools/cudafy_*.py).
	* cu_ symbol namespace (tools/cu_prefix.py) for coexistence with the
	  system libgmp/libmpfr/libmpc.
	* Device-correct mpz-based mpfr_div; full transcendental support.
	* Per-thread bump arena and grid-stride launch.
	* Demos/benchmarks: AXPY, matrix-vector, matrix-matrix, and elementary
	  function benchmarks for MPFR and MPC.
	* autoconf-based build system; Markdown manual under doc/.
